// W4e surface fold-in — shell subshell grouping (parse-only fixture).
//
// GRADUATION: the shell DSL's subshell `[ … ]` is a real molded form again
// (wyrd-83wx). W4c had folded it away because its `[` opener competed with the
// host list literal at every `[`; W4e reintroduces it on DISTINCT shell-context
// bracket tiles (emitted only inside a shell block), so the host list-literal
// `[` menu is untouched and the form is genuinely moldable — not a dead rule.
//
// DIVERGENCE from POSIX sh: the gandr shell dialect spells a subshell `[ … ]`
// (the committed tree-sitter `subshell`), NOT the POSIX `( … )` — `[` is the
// POSIX `test` builtin, and `( … )` is kept free for the `$( … )` host escape.
// The SEMANTICS (running the group in a child world) graduate under the
// wyrd-83wx gandr-shell wiring follow-up. Parse-only; never lowered.

// A subshell groups a `;`-separated command list.
#!{ [ cd build; ls ]; }

// A single-command subshell.
#!{ [ echo hi ]; }

// Subshells compose with the pipeline and list operators like any command.
#!{ [ cd src; grep foo ] | sort; }

// Nested subshells.
#!{ [ echo outer; [ echo inner ] ]; }
